host Ubuntu cloud pier — Eastern (EDT) time convention
title HUNK16 — the edit cursor: undo and redo over one history (edit_cursor.rye)
prompt Autonomous recursion lap: continue the Season-A Photos journey Lindy-first crux-first after HUNK15 sent; take the next agent-doable crux, land a clean self-contained increment, send it as its own signed round, stop at custody gates.
think After HUNK15 (the Skate view of a revert) the named next-crux options were another Photos verb (hue/saturation, a smoother resampler), a revert/redo cursor over the edit-list, or another season. Lindy-first crux-first chose the cursor: undo/redo is the durable capability every editing surface wants once, not a seventh pixel verb padding the count. Crux-first, its hard-but-solvable move (a fresh edit while rewound forgets the redo tail) is the one design decision that makes a cursor more than two counters.
think Read the model before building: photo_edits.rye (HUNK11) gives EditList + apply + render/parse; photo_revert.rye (HUNK14) gives truncate — pure over the count, returning a fresh shorter list. The cursor is exactly one EditList plus a u32 position with the invariant position <= count. applied = truncate(list, position); view = apply(source, applied); push truncates to position then appends (forgetting the tail); undo/redo clamp. No new storage, no new error class.
think Wrote the self-approved design round first (active-designing/20260813-171500_…), then image/edit_cursor.rye with the opening triad, >=2 asserts per fn each with a positive // invariant:, then the witness mirroring HUNK14's grep shape.
obs Proofs make correctness unambiguous over a 6×6 coordinate-tagged image (matching photo_edits/photo_revert's own craft so by-hand replays line up): undo-to-2 equals the first two verbs by hand, redo returns byte-for-byte, a full rewind to the original then rolls every step forward unchanged, the crux (rewind-one then push flip_h forgets the +40 adjust, the new road = crop·rotate·flip_h by hand), both edges clamp, the applied prefix still round-trips as an open record, the 64-edit ceiling refuses TooManyEdits.
obs One honesty fix before send: the GREEN line first printed at2.width (=4, the cropped image width) where it read "undo to {d}"; captured undo_pos (=2) so the printed number is the cursor position it claims, not a coincidental image dimension.
obs No custody gate reached — a pure look and pure move over the edit-list; no name, no bead, no key, no funds, no network. HUNK11 and HUNK14 witnesses still GREEN beneath (imported, their files untouched); no new symlink needed (edit_cursor reuses image/'s existing links).
loom witness=hunk_edit_cursor_witness image=6x6 history_edits=3 ceiling=64 result=GREEN
file image/edit_cursor.rye HUNK16 — EditCursor (list + position); undo/redo/push/applied/view; a fresh edit forgets the redo tail; selftest GREEN.
file tools/hunk_edit_cursor_witness.rish witnesses HUNK16 on metal (walk both ways · forget-tail · clamp · open-record round-trip).
file active-designing/20260813-171500_hunk-edit-cursor-undo-redo-exploration.md self-approved design round naming the crux and the value model.
file work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md latest-lap bumped with the HUNK16 landing; git nib refreshed in the same work commit.
recommend keep-going — next agent-doable crux is another Photos gesture (bilinear/area resampler, or hue/saturation as a bounded verb), the cursor painted through Skate (a dimmed redo tail) or beaded into Tablecloth as a live session, or another Season-A / double-seat journey; all agent-doable, no gate.
